    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d624">

                <pb facs="0672" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.5200 Compañia Terrenos Y Ganados San
                    Rodrigo/29: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-11T21:00:00-06:00">December 11,
                            1939—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. Referring to the Department’s telegram No. 244, December 11, 5 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="22" xml:id="d624-f1"/> Lie. Mena, Chief of the Diplomatic Section,
                    informed Gibson<anchor n="23" xml:id="d624-f2"/> that possession would not be
                    given December 12th and that the 30-day period for fencing had been granted.
                    American Consul at Piedras Negras informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
